<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<jcr:root xmlns:jcr="http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0"
          xmlns:kes="http://kestros.io/kes/1.0"
          xmlns:mix="http://www.jcp.org/jcr/mix/1.0"
          xmlns:nt="http://www.jcp.org/jcr/nt/1.0"
          xmlns:rep="http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0"
          xmlns:sling="http://sling.apache.org/jcr/sling/1.0"
          jcr:primaryType="kes:Page"
>
    <jcr:content
            jcr:description="Not nostalgia. The constraint of a pencil on paper is still the fastest way to think through a building."
            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
            jcr:title="Why we still draw by hand at the start of every project"
            kes:template="/libs/kestros/commons/base-site-template"
            sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/kestros-base-page"
    >
        <header
                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/inherited-content-area"
        />
        <main
                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/content-area"
        >
            <hero
                    inlineVariations="uk-section uk-section-primary"
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/section"
            >
                <container
                        inlineVariations="uk-container"
                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                        sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/container"
                >
                    <meta
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-meta uk-text-uppercase"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="February 2024. M. Haven."
                    />
                    <heading
                            headingText="Why we still draw by hand at the start of every project"
                            headingType="h1"
                            inlineVariations="uk-heading-medium"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/heading"
                    />
                    <dek
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="Not nostalgia. The constraint of a pencil on paper is still the fastest way to think through a building."
                    />
                </container>
            </hero>
            <body
                    inlineVariations="uk-section uk-section-default"
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/section"
            >
                <container
                        inlineVariations="uk-container"
                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                        sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/container"
                >
                    <p0
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="We use the same computer tools as everyone else. When it comes time to document a building we have the models, the BIM, the engineering coordination. That is not in question."
                    />
                    <p1
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="But for the first four or five weeks of a project, before the consultants are on board and before the site has been properly measured, we work almost entirely in plan sketches, section studies, and the occasional small chipboard model. The reason is not nostalgia. It is that the pencil imposes a cost on every line. You have to commit to a move before you draw it, because undoing a pencil line is a minor defeat."
                    />
                    <p2
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="That cost is what we are paying for. It is the reason the first conversation with a client goes better at a table with a sheet of tracing paper on it than it does at a screen. The sketch is slow enough to think with."
                    />
                </container>
            </body>
        </main>
        <footer
                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/inherited-content-area"
        />
    </jcr:content>
</jcr:root>
